republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/two-senses: P3 (S26): "more" is taken as seeks to exceed the unlike, but not the like, in the practice of a skill in P3 C1 and as seeks advantage or gain over the unlike but not over the like where unlike_only is used else, a reader says: the argument does not turn on it
republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/two-senses: P4 (S29): "more" is taken as seeks to exceed everyone, like and unlike, in the practice of a skill in P4 C2 and as seeks advantage or gain over everyone, like and unlike where both is used else, a reader says: the argument does not turn on it
republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: A2: it takes "more" from exceeding others in the practice of a skill to seeking advantage or gain over others, a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r3.sense3)
republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another}; bad = ∅, both = {another}, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, just = ∅, like_ignorant = ∅, like_wise = ∅, unjust = {another}, unlike_only = ∅, wise = ∅
